# Review Notes

## Summary
T064: `oal report` no longer warns OAL-REPORT-TERMINAL-FROM-LEDGER on
healthy batches. The diagnostic now fires only when the ledger terminal
and run.completed.json disagree, or the ledger record is missing.

## Observations
- Agreement rule: disposition, censor_class, and evidence_integrity are
  compared where both records carry a string. At least one compared
  field and no differences yields verified; any difference yields
  conflict; a missing ledger record or a missing completion record
  stays unverified and warns.
- Verified projections keep the stable diagnostic code at severity info
  in JSON output, suppressed under --quiet; terminal and markdown stay
  quiet outside --verbose.
- The dead fromLedger counter left assignmentsOf with no other
  consumer; removal swept clean across packages and apps.

## Accepted findings (recorded, not blocking)
- One-sided agreement: a field present on only one side is skipped, so
  a ledger censor_class against a deleted completion censor_class
  classifies as verified. Within the "where present" rule; both runner
  writer paths always emit all three fields, and tampering hits the
  artifact drift gate. No test pins the shape.
- Under --verbose --quiet the info diagnostic is suppressed while other
  info diagnostics treat --verbose as authoritative. Contradictory-flag
  edge with no pinned semantics.

## Verdict
Approved — landed unchanged (review verdicts land/land, zero blockers).
